      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?",
      "worked_solution": "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4$\n\nLet's first rearrange our inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{4}<1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that this represents an ellipse centered at $O$ with semi-axes $2$ and $1.$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253115/assets/fdb0a299dd6ee0bd58ceb1a74c9423bf5cac81857b0538dcda7f0a4cba9a1108.png)",
